# QB64pe Project

QB64 Phoenix Edition is a self-hosted BASIC compiler: QB64 source → C++ → native executable. Compiler is in QB64 (bootstrapped).

## Build

- **Setup**: `./setup_lnx.sh` (Linux), `./setup_osx.command` (macOS), `./setup_win.cmd` (Windows)
- **Compile a program**: `./qb64pe -x yourfile.bas` or `./qb64pe -c yourfile.bas -o output.exe`
- **Build QB64pe itself**: `./qb64pe -x ./source/qb64pe.bas`
- **Make** (usually invoked by QB64pe): `make OS=lnx EXE=program BUILD_QB64=y`; use `DEP_*` for deps (e.g. `DEP_GL`, `DEP_AUDIO_MINIAUDIO`)

## Test

- `tests/run_tests.sh` — QB64 + format + add-prefix
- `tests/compile_tests.sh` — compiler/language tests
- `tests/compile_tests/`: `*.bas` + `*.output` (expected stdout) or `*.err` (expected error); optional `*.flags`, `*.compile-from-base`

## Layout

- `source/qb64pe.bas` — main compiler; `source/ide/` — IDE; `source/subs_functions/` — built-ins; `source/utilities/` — compiler utils
- `internal/c/libqb/` — C++ runtime; `internal/c/parts/` — third-party; `internal/source/` — pre-generated C++ (bootstrap); `internal/temp/` — generated C++

